  "term": "Deplin",
  "definition": "Deplin refers to levomefolic acid, a nutritional supplement containing L-methylfolate, the biologically active form of vitamin B9. In the supplied source, it is described as having possible anti-cancer effects through effects on DNA methylation and tumor cell growth, and as being able to cross the blood-brain barrier.",
